DESCRIPTION:P1 · Proof & Strategy Base · week 1 of 178\nWed Aug 19 2026
  → Sun Aug 23 2026\n\nZeitz ch.1 (What is problem solving?) + Book of 
 Proof ch.1–2 · P&B ch.1 opens\n◆ DAY 1 = Wed 19 Aug (Wed–Sun stub
  week). Baseline diagnostic. Both logs open. SAT thread begins.\n\nDEEP 
 BLOCK (09:15\, Mon/Tue/Wed/Fri · 07:30 Thu)\nZeitz ch.1 — what proble
 m solving actually is: exercise vs. problem\, and the psychology of the 
 20-minute struggle. CONCEPT FIRST: read with pen in hand\, work every ex
 ample BEFORE its solution\, 20-minute struggle rule. Zeitz is not a book
  you read\; it is a book you argue with.\n\nBLOCK B (13:00)\nP&B §1.1 (
 Argument by Contradiction) — 5–6 problems matched to this week's the
 ory\, full write-ups. PLUS the proof on-ramp this week: Book of Proof pp
 .15–27 (§1.1–1.3 Sets: Introduction to Sets\, The Cartesian Product
 \, Subsets) — 3 content days\, ~4 pages/day. Pace it across the week's
  content days\; do not try to do it all in one sitting.\n\nSLOT C + jour
 nal (15:30)\nSAT thread STARTS (slot C\, 30–40 min\, hard cap): Bluebo
 ok diagnostic + Meltzer Grammar pp.7–15 (Intro\, Cheat Sheet\, Parts o
 f Speech\, Preliminary Exercise) — the SAT is a distributed thread in 
 slot C only\; keep it to the dose and it never touches the deep block. T
 hen the journal: key idea / where stuck / technique tag for every proble
 m attempted today.\n\nSATURDAY SIMULATION (09:00)\nBASELINE DIAGNOSTIC 
 — Putnam 2001 A1 + B1\, untimed\, take as long as you need. Write real
  proofs\, not sketches. Then grade against the official solution with th
 e hostile rubric. Whatever number comes out is the honest floor you are 
 building from — record it.
END:VEVENT
